{"name":"Eye Patch","hex":"#232121","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eye patch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An opaque patch worn so as to cover an injured or infected eye or an eye socket in order to protect or conceal it, or to treat amblyopia in children."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eye_patch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eyepatch","blocks":[{"text":"An eyepatch is a small patch that is worn in front of one eye. It may be a cloth patch attached around the head by an elastic band or by a string, an adhesive bandage, or a plastic device which is clipped to a pair of glasses. It is often worn by people to cover a lost, infected, or injured eye, but it also has a therapeutic use in children for the treatment of amblyopia. Eyepatches used to block light while sleeping are referred to as a sleep mask."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Child_eyepatch.jpg/330px-Child_eyepatch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eyepatch","wikidata":"Q760330"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye","wikidata":"Q7364"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Two_sailors_with_amputated_legs%2C_an_eyepatch_and_an_amputate_Wellcome_V0020360.jpg/500px-Two_sailors_with_amputated_legs%2C_an_eyepatch_and_an_amputate_Wellcome_V0020360.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Two_sailor